{
	"Name": "Okta - Authentication & Sessions - Okta OAuth Refresh Token Reuse Detected",
	"Description": "Alert: Alert - Okta - Authentication & Sessions\nMITRE ATT&CK: Credential Access / T1528\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Okta OAuth Refresh Token Reuse Detected\" or \"<ip>|Okta OAuth Refresh Token Reuse Detected\"\n\nOkta detected an already-used (rotated) OAuth refresh token being presented again (app.oauth2.token.detect_reuse for the org authorization server, app.oauth2.as.token.detect_reuse for custom authorization servers). With refresh token rotation, reuse means two parties hold the same token: a strong sign the token was stolen. Okta revokes the token family; review the client and user.",
